## What to hunt for beyond that

<% if dimension -%>
- alternation branches with no corpus case — spelled-out forms, abbreviations, separator variants
- `match` arms and `if let` branches in value construction that no case reaches
- boundary and sign handling: negatives, zero, very large values, decimal and thousands separators
- value-shape fields the corpus never asserts on, which would let a wrong shape pass
<% else -%>
- `match` arms and `if let` branches in the **resolver** that no corpus text reaches — the sweep only sees rule patterns, never `mod.rs`
- boundary values the corpus only samples (`DayOfWeek` 0..6, `Month` 1..12, `DayOfMonth` 1..31, `Season` 0..3, negative `n`)
- `Option` fields resolving to `None` where the corpus only supplies `Some` — `DateMDY`'s `year`, `Holiday`'s year
- grain interactions: which `Grain` this slice reports, and how `early_late` or a `direction` changes it
<% end -%>
- rules whose pattern is pure `predicate`/`dim` composition, which the sweep cannot see at all

